    <innerclass refid="classDatabaseConnectionPool" prot="public">DatabaseConnectionPool</innerclass>
    <briefdescription>
<para>Owns the fixed set of synchronous <ref refid="classDatabase" kindref="compound">Database</ref> connections and leases them to callers. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This header declares <ref refid="classDatabaseConnectionPool" kindref="compound">DatabaseConnectionPool</ref>, the manager for a fixed number of <ref refid="classDatabase" kindref="compound">Database</ref> objects. It builds every connection up front at startup, stores idle ones in a <ref refid="classBlockingPool" kindref="compound">BlockingPool</ref>, leases them with get_connection(), and takes them back with return_connection(). It also exposes reconnect_all() to refresh idle links after a database outage, and emits warnings when the pool is saturated.</para>
<para>WHY THIS FILE MATTERS IN THE SERVER: The pool is the gatekeeper for the server&apos;s synchronous database capacity. Controllers and the watchdog do not create connections themselves; <ref refid="classDatabaseHanndler" kindref="compound">DatabaseHanndler</ref> leases one from here for each request, and the HTTP layer turns a timeout into 503 when no connection is free. The pool reads its size and timeout from Configurator, and delegates the actual hand-out/return mechanics to <ref refid="classBlockingPool" kindref="compound">BlockingPool</ref>. Without it, every request would open its own connection, which is slow, unbounded, and would exhaust the database&apos;s connection limit.</para>
<para>CONCEPTS TO LEARN (for beginners):<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>RAII (a lease is acquired in a constructor and returned in a destructor): <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/raii">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/raii</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>std::atomic (a value safe to read/write from several threads): <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/atomic/atomic">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/atomic/atomic</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>std::chrono (time points and durations): <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/chrono">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/chrono</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>std::shared_ptr (shared ownership of an object): <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/shared_ptr">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/shared_ptr</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Exception specifications via <parameterlist kind="exception"><parameteritem>
